adr: 0215
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: typeinquiry
why: AP 6.4.9's containment is by construction: a bare name is put back in tqAt/tqLen, so a conforming program takes 6.4.9's own path under --std=afterschool and every rule the clause already had is asked the question it was written for. Sending a bare name down the access path instead looks harmless -- InquiryOfAccess answers the same type for `type of n` -- and it is not: the closest-containing rule, the schematic-formal refusal and the slice refusal are all written against tqAt/tqLen and stop being asked. dialect-containment is what notices, over the whole conformance corpus compiled a second way; the dialect's own cases stay green, because every one of them writes a selector.
--- old
            if obj^.kind = nkVar then begin
              t^.tqAt := obj^.vrAt;
              t^.tqLen := obj^.vrLen
            end
            else
              t^.tqObj := obj
--- new
            t^.tqObj := obj
